  "$comment": "Fleet Tier-1 (qa-runner, dev-engineer): Tier-0 plus verification gates, fleet/* branch pushes, PR creation, beta deploy, and code edits — but read the next sentence before trusting that last one. The code-edit allow targets /var/www/vhosts/kalfa.me/beta-fleet, a worktree that DOES NOT EXIST (verified 2026-07-29 against `git worktree list`; it is still an open owner decision in .claude/fleet/TODO.md). So today that rule matches nothing, the only writable path at this tier is .fleet-logs, and qa-runner — the one ENABLED Tier-1 role — neither needs nor uses it: its prompt forbids editing code at all. The consequence worth knowing: `git worktree add` would silently activate full write access to a complete repo copy WITHOUT any permission file changing, so creating that directory IS the permission decision. Every prod-DB / secrets / infra deny from Tier-0 stays. File-path rules use Edit(path)/Read(path) forms only — Edit(path) is what grants/denies the Write tool too (Write(path) rules are never matched; verified against July 2026 docs). Deny beats allow, so the .claude/fleet + agent_configs denies carve those out of the worktree allow once it exists.",
